tput schema: mst_edges array of arrays with exactly 3 elements: string, string, number. total_weight number. Good.\n\nMake sure to not mutate input case (even though not required). Use list/set copies.\n\nNow write the implementation string. Must be valid Python.\n\nWe'll also handle potential missing nodes? But payload is valid.\n\nWrite solve function that accepts case dict and returns dict.\n\nNow produce final answer: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    edge_map = {}\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        edge_map[(u, v)] = d\\n    edges = []\\n    for (u, v), d in edge_map.items():\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst = []\\n    total = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst.append([u, v, w])\\n            total += w\\n            if len(mst) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('input graph is disconnected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst, 'total_weight': total}\"}\n\nWe need to escape newlines and quotes for JSON. Use json.dumps on the entire implementation string. But the final response is a JSON object with key \"implementation\". We'll construct